    "content": "{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Improve memory locality and loop order by using a blocked approach to process submatrices in larger chunks.\",\n  \"transformations\": [\"Reorganize the matrix processing to use blocking for better cache utilization.\", \"Adjust loop order to enhance spatial locality.\"],\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\",\n      \"content\": \"#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n#include <cstdio>\\n#include <cassert>\\n#include <climits>\\n\\nint main() {\\n\\tint n, s;\\n\\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\\n\\tstd::vector<std::vector<int>> matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\\n\\tfor (int i = 0; i < n; i++)\\n\\t\\tfor (int j = 0; j < n; j++) \\n\\t\\t\\tscanf(\\\"%d\\\", &(matrix[i][j]));\\n\\n\\tassert(s < n);\\n\\tassert(n < 8000);\\n\\tassert(s > 0);\\n\\tassert(n > 0);\\n\\n\\tint blockSize = 32; // Define a block size for better cache utilization\\n\\tint mxSum = INT_MIN;\\n\\n\\tfor (int bi = 0; bi < n; bi += blockSize) {\\n\\t\\tfor (int bj = 0; bj < n; bj += blockSize) {\\n\\t\\t\\tint sum = 0;\\n\\t\\t\\tfor (int i = bi; i < std::min(bi + blockSize, n); i++) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tfor (int j = bj; j < std::min(bj + blockSize, n); j++) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif (i < s && j < s) { // Only consider the initial block for the first submatrix\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tsum += matrix[i][j];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tmxSum = std::max(mxSum, sum);\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tfor (int i = bi; i < n - s + 1; i++) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif (i > bi) { // Slide the block down by one row\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tfor (int j = bj; j < std::min(bj + blockSize, n); j++) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tsum -= matrix[i - s][j];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif (i + s < n) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tsum += matrix[i][j];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tfor (int j = bj; j < n - s + 1; j++) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif (j > bj) { // Slide the block right by one column\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tsum -= matrix[i][j - s];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif (j + s < n) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tsum += matrix[i][j];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tmxSum = std::max(mxSum, sum);\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tprintf(\\\"%d\\\\n\\\", mxSum);\\n}\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"This experiment introduces a blocked approach to process submatrices in larger chunks, which can improve memory locality and cache utilization. The loop order is adjusted to enhance spatial locality by processing blocks of the matrix before sliding them.\"\n}"
